From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:37:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: keep SEG_ADD.i64 src[1] out of the low destination
 register

SEG_ADD.i64 is lowered by the scheduler into *SEG_ADD (writes the low
half of the destination) and +SEG_ADD in the same tuple (reads src[1],
writes the high half). The ADD's read of a register written by the FMA
of its tuple is rewritten to the stage passthrough, so when RA put src[1]
in the same register as the low destination half, the high half became
SEG_ADD(low result) instead of SEG_ADD(0) and the atomic went to a wrong
address.

This happens when the WLS offset is a uniform (an OpenCL __local kernel
argument): the #0 high half then has to be moved to a register because
the tuple's FAU slot is taken. Every __local atomic except xchg/cmpxchg
returned 0 and left memory untouched (OpenCL-CTS atomics: atomic_add,
sub, min, max, inc, dec, xor; C11 atomic_fetch_add/sub/xor/min/max).

Add an interference between the destination and src[1].

Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
index abcc2f8b09d..dd964de9a04 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
@@ -393,6 +393,23 @@ bi_mark_interference(bi_block *block, struct lcra_state *l, uint8_t *live,
          }
       }
 
+      /* SEG_ADD.i64 is lowered at scheduling time to *SEG_ADD, which writes
+       * the low half of the destination, and +SEG_ADD in the same tuple,
+       * which reads src[1] and writes the high half. A read by the ADD of a
+       * register written by the FMA of its tuple is rewritten to the stage
+       * passthrough, so if src[1] shared a register with the low half of the
+       * destination, the ADD would see the new low half instead of src[1].
+       * This happens when src[0] is a uniform and the #0 high half had to be
+       * moved to a register, e.g. OpenCL __local kernel arguments, and broke
+       * every __local atomic except xchg. Keep them apart.
+       */
+      if (ins->op == BI_OPCODE_SEG_ADD_I64 && bi_is_ssa(ins->src[1]) &&
+          bi_is_ssa(ins->dest[0])) {
+         lcra_add_node_interference(l, ins->dest[0].value, bi_writemask(ins, 0),
+                                    ins->src[1].value,
+                                    BITFIELD_BIT(ins->src[1].offset));
+      }
+
       /* Valhall needs >= 64-bit reads to be pair-aligned */
       if (aligned_sr) {
          bi_foreach_ssa_src(ins, s) {
